WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960
"One of the Most Effective Single Pieces
of Advice for Weight Loss"

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.800
How does the fiber
we eat in foods

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.520
impact our appetites
and our resting metabolic rate,

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.800
the amount of calories burned
just by existing?

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.720
What happens when we eat
fiber-filled foods like beans?

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.920
Researchers in Sweden gave
people beans for supper,

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.280
and by the next morning,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.240
after their friendly flora had
a chance to eat them too,

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.280
their satiety hormones
like PYY were up,

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.000
their hunger hormone ghrelin
was down,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.760
and they reported
feeling less hungry.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.560
The researchers didn’t measure
subsequent food intake,

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.560
but a similar study with
whole-grain rye for supper did

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.920
and found a decrease in food
intake at lunch the next day.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.480
Those who had eaten the
fiber-rich food the night before

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.480
felt fully satiated with about a
hundred fewer calories at a meal

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.360
more than 12 hours later.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.960
So, by eating fiber-rich foods,

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.400
you’re setting yourself up
for success.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.400
Reduced caloric intake
at a single meal,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.080
or even over a whole day,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.120
doesn’t necessarily translate

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.960
into long-term weight loss,
though,

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.800
as our body may find
ways of compensating.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.880
Experimentally delivering
short-chain fatty acids

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.120
directly to the colon
every day for months

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.280
does reduce abdominal fat,
liver fat,

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.880
and overall weight gain.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.520
But what about getting them
the old-fashioned way,

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.760
eating fiber through our mouth?

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.680
A 2022 systematic review
and meta-analysis compilation

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.240
of more than two dozen
randomized controlled trials

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.080
of various straight fiber
supplements versus placebo

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.520
found that those
study participants

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.080
in the groups taking
the actual fiber

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.560
lost an average of about two
and a half pounds (1.25 kg) more

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.000
than those
in the control groups.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.960
These were studies only
averaging 17 weeks long,

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.960
though there have been fiber
supplementation trials

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.640
that have lasted up to a year,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.120
and they showed
significantly more weight loss.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.760
The fiber supplement findings
were inconsistent, however,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.320
presumably because dozens
of different fiber types

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.920
were tested.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.280
How much money can you make
selling beans?

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.760
So, there are all sorts of fancy
new fibers on the market

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.000
with names like "IQP G-002AS."

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.320
(The IQP stands for InQpharm,

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.720
the drug company
that came up with it.)

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.120
Ironically, it was found
to be quite effective--

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.240
according, of course, to the
employees of said drug company,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.720
who published the study.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.200
Using isolated fiber
extracted from plants

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.240
or made in a lab

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.440
can be helpful in experimentally
proving fiber’s effectiveness

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.360
apart from all the other healthy
components in whole foods.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.080
But if anything, one might
expect even greater benefits

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.160
from eating fiber
the way nature intended,

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.400
in intact plant foods.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.760
It turns out that telling people

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.600
to increase their intake
of fiber-rich foods

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.200
may actually be
one of the most effective

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.400
single pieces of advice
for weight loss.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.800
Published in the prestigious
Annals of Internal Medicine,

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:53.840
a study entitled

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.040
"Single-Component Versus
Multicomponent Dietary Goals"

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.800
randomly assigned
hundreds of people

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.000
into one of two
weight-loss regimens.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.200
One simply encouraged people

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.080
to get at least 30 grams
of fiber each day,

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.120
which is about the recommended
minimum adequate intake.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.400
The other group was advised

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.960
to follow a far more complex
weight-loss program

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.920
recommended by
the American Heart Association.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.840
In addition to also
being advised to hit

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.400
the 30 daily grams of fiber
target,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.000
study participants
were prescribed

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.400
carefully calculated
calorie intake goals,

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.200
told to switch
from red meat to white,

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.880
cut down on sugary beverages,

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.440
reduce sugar and sodium intake
across the board,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.440
and moderate
their alcohol intake.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.800
Even though
both groups were told

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.640
to reach the same fiber target,

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.960
the group whose sole focus
was fiber intake

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.440
ended up eating more than
twice as much extra fiber

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.920
as the multicomponent
intervention,

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.200
and surprisingly,

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.240
similarly improved
the quality of their diets.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.480
So, the fiber-only group
ended up reducing

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.640
their saturated fat intake
as much as the group

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:57.280
who was explicitly
instructed to do so.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.360
Just telling people
to eat more whole plant foods

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.840
seems by default
to naturally crowd out

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.600
some of the less healthy options

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:08.080
that may have ended up
on their plates.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.840
With similar
dietary improvements,

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.160
both groups lost
similar amounts of weight,

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.200
suggesting if you were able

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.840
to give only one piece
of weight-loss advice,

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:19.280
eating more fiber
might not be a bad choice.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.080
Of course, it only works
if you actually do it.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.640
One low-carb study reported
favorable results

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.360
compared to a "high-fiber" diet.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:31.040
How high was this so-called
high-fiber diet?

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.480
The study participants
started out

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:36.160
at a terribly low
17.4 grams a day.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.120
Unfortunately, that’s pretty
typical for the United States.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.040
That’s only about half
the average recommended

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.800
minimum daily intake
of 31.5 grams.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.720
The human body
was designed to consume

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.200
more than 100 grams of fiber
a day.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:52.640
The participants started out
at 17.4 grams,

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:58.400
and on their "high-fiber" diet,
shot up to 19.7 grams.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.120
That is in no way
a high-fiber diet,

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.760
yet the researchers used
their findings to conclude,

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:06.160
"we believe previous claims
of the benefits of fiber

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.960
for weight loss
may have been overstated."

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.680
Less than 3% of Americans
reach even the recommended

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.160
minimum daily
adequate intake of fiber.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.160
There’s so much fuss
about protein,

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.640
but for that,
the stats are reversed:

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.920
More than 97% of Americans
do get enough protein,

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:26.880
and more than 97% of Americans
do not get enough fiber.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.440
Almost everyone is eating
fiber-deficient diets,

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.400
and that’s just based

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.280
on the piddly U.S.
dietary recommendations

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.920
of 14 grams
per thousand calories,

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:39.520
which comes out to be
about 25 g/day for women

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.886
and 38 g/day for men.

